{
 "id": "Chart3D",
 "name": "chart-3d",
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Chart3D",
 "prompt": "Show monthly rainfall for London, Seattle and Mumbai from January to June as 3D bars I can turn, and below it the saddle z = x² − y² as a 3D surface.",
 "level": 3,
 "use_cases": [
  "chart"
 ],
 "form_factor": "phone",
 "keywords": [
  "3d chart",
  "3d bar chart",
  "3d bars",
  "3d scatter",
  "scatter plot 3d",
  "bubble chart 3d",
  "3d surface",
  "surface plot",
  "z = f(x, y)",
  "function of two variables",
  "height map",
  "orbit",
  "drag to rotate",
  "rainfall",
  "saddle"
 ],
 "teaches": [
  "Data, not geometry: {\"Chart3D\": {\"categories\": [...], \"series\": [...], \"values\": [[...], ...]}} gives 3D bars; {\"fn\": \"x^2 - y^2\", \"x\": [-2, 2]} a surface; points [[x, y, z], ...] a scatter. The server picks round ranges and ticks and frames the camera",
  "Floor and back walls carry gridlines on the ticks; the wall facing the camera is culled, so the back two always show as it turns",
  "Labels are 2D text at projected points, computed at run time from the same spin and tilt as the 3D pass: they follow the orbit and stay sharp",
  "Bars take the theme's series colours in a fixed order and a legend; a surface and a scatter take a five-step blue ramp by height (one mesh per step); mono draws boxes with edges and a hidden-line wireframe"
 ],
 "pitfalls": [
  "3D support has not landed in androidx yet (coming): this plays in the C++ and TypeScript players only. Don't use it for a screen that must play on Android today"
 ],
 "java_difference": "3D operations: not in the Java JSON parser or androidx remote-core yet; 3D support has not landed in androidx yet (coming); plays in the C++ and TypeScript players",
